{"name":"Sin City","hex":"#cfa236","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sin City","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Nickname for Las Vegas: a desert city, the county seat of Clark County, Nevada, United States.","Nickname for Pattaya: a resort city in Chonburi Province, Thailand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sin_City"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sin City","blocks":[{"text":"Sin City is a series of neo-noir comics by American comic book writer-artist Frank Miller. The first story originally appeared in Dark Horse Presents Fifth Anniversary Special, and continued in Dark Horse Presents 51–62 from May 1991 to June 1992, under the title of Sin City, serialized in thirteen parts. Several other stories of variable lengths have followed. The intertwining stories, with frequently recurring characters, take place in Basin City."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/Sin_City_Hard_Goodbye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sin_City"},{"title":"Sin City (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sin City is a 2005 American neo-noir crime anthology film directed by Robert Rodriguez and Frank Miller based on Miller's comic book series of the same name. The film stars an ensemble cast led by Jessica Alba, Benicio del Toro, Brittany Murphy, Clive Owen, Mickey Rourke, Bruce Willis, Michael Clarke Duncan and Elijah Wood, and featuring Alexis Bledel, Powers Boothe, Rosario Dawson, Devon Aoki, Carla Gugino, Josh Hartnett, Rutger Hauer, Jaime King, Michael Madsen, Nick Stahl, and Makenzie Vega among others."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Sincitypostercast.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sin_City_(film)"},{"title":"Sin","blocks":[{"text":"The term sin originates from the Old English word synn, tracing back to Proto-Germanic and Proto-Indo-European roots meaning \"being\" or \"truly guilty\", implying a judgment of wrongdoing. Over time, different religions and cultures developed distinct understandings of sin, often shaping moral frameworks and spiritual practices. Each culture has its own interpretation of what it means to commit a sin. While sins are generally considered actions, any thought, word, or act considered immoral, amoral, selfish, shameful, harmful, or alienating might be termed \"sinful\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Jan_Brueghel_de_Oude_en_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Het_aards_paradijs_met_de_zondeval_van_Adam_en_Eva.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_de_Oude_en_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Het_aards_paradijs_met_de_zondeval_van_Adam_en_Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sin"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Hard_Goodbye.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/Hard_Goodbye.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An example of Frank Miller's use of high contrasts in Sin City","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHard_Goodbye.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg/500px-Bruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg/1280px-Bruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg/500px-Bruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABruce_Willis_by_Gage_Skidmore_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mickey_Rourke_10_December_2010_%28cropped%29.jpeg/500px-Mickey_Rourke_10_December_2010_%28cropped%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mickey_Rourke_10_December_2010_%28cropped%29.jpeg/500px-Mickey_Rourke_10_December_2010_%28cropped%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMickey_Rourke_10_December_2010_(cropped).jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Clive_Owen_%28Children_of_men%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Clive_Owen_%28Children_of_men%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wik